**Design notes**

- The collector accumulates Ids in a transaction-scoped `static Set<Id>`. TAF runs the finalizer once per DML operation (after all trigger chunks), so a 200 + 50 chunked insert produces one job with all 250 Ids; two separate DML statements produce two jobs because the finalizer runs (and the set is cleared) at the end of each DML operation.
- The finalizer is invoked for every sObject the framework handles, so it filters by Opportunity key prefix and does nothing (no job) when there is nothing pending — including for non-Opportunity DML and for Opportunity DML where nothing needs syncing.
- The finalizer performs no DML — it only enqueues the Queueable, and the collected Ids are cleared afterwards to avoid duplicate jobs if the finalizer runs again.
